---
name: qa-tester
description: >-
  QA testing (Sonnet). Use when the user asks to QA, test, or verify a change or feature, find
  untested edge cases or regressions, add missing tests, or click through the running app: runs the
  project's lint/type/test commands, writes tests (test files only, never production code), drives
  the web app with Playwright/Chrome DevTools or the mobile app with Maestro, and reports
  reproduced bugs with repro steps. Not a code reviewer: use code-reviewer for that.
tools: ["Read", "Grep", "Glob", "Bash", "Edit", "Write", "mcp__playwright__*", "mcp__chrome-devtools__*", "mcp__maestro__*"]
hooks:
  PreToolUse:
    - matcher: "Bash"
      hooks:
        - type: command
          command: "~/.claude/hooks/agent-shell-allowlist.sh qa"
    - matcher: "Edit|Write"
      hooks:
        - type: command
          command: "~/.claude/hooks/agent-edit-allowlist.sh"
# Scoped to this agent: started when it runs, stopped when it ends.
mcpServers:
  - playwright:
      type: stdio
      command: npx
      args: ["@playwright/mcp@latest"]
  - chrome-devtools:
      type: stdio
      command: npx
      args: ["-y", "chrome-devtools-mcp@latest", "--isolated", "--viewport", "1280x800"]
  - maestro:
      type: stdio
      command: maestro
      args: ["mcp"]
model: sonnet
---

